frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point $P$ lies in the second quadrant, we subtract the reference angle from $\\pi $ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are $(2,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289722 13194139534465 true] [17592186289721 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534465 true] [17592186289721 1041 "field-1" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289721 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289722 13194139534465 true] [17592186289721 1110 #uuid "429509a8-b66f-5a5e-ad6d-c517ad9ac724" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289722 1034 "2" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534465 true] [17592186289722 1111 #uuid "1f76cb9a-40f1-5c3f-a9d4-4cf44f1d6914" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289724 13194139534465 true] [17592186289723 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534465 true] [17592186289723 1041 "field-2" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289723 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289724 13194139534465 true] [17592186289723 1110 #uuid "898b994b-0c53-59f3-94e6-7fea00cc240e" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289724 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534465 true] [17592186289724 1111 #uuid "9bedf116-1ecb-5f35-8da3-7700073366f8" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289726 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1089 "q-40756" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1100 "A point $P$ has Cartesian coordinates $(0,12).$ What are the polar coordinates of $P?$" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1113 #uuid "501b4a98-609b-5b94-8408-270235db8b79" 13194139534465 true] [17592186289725 1145 "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sq